.env
.DS_Store
.claude/*
# The repo's own skills are shared with every session on the repo
# (docs/photo-labels.md §6), and so are its hooks and agents and the
# settings.json that registers them: the cloud session that needs the
# SessionStart hook is exactly the one that has no machine of its own.
# settings.local.json and the rest stay one machine's.
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/settings.json
.playwright-mcp/
*.jpeg
data/.env
data/node_modules/
# The root one, which had no rule at all. `data/` and `dashboard/` were
# listed and `app/` has its own file, so the gap only showed once something
# put a `node_modules/` at the top level — and by then a vitest results
# cache had already been committed from inside it.
node_modules/
data/review/.cache/
dashboard/node_modules/
dashboard/dist/
dashboard/.env.local
# Supabase CLI scratch state — a cache marker it writes on any invocation,
# including the `functions deploy` this repo has no workflow for. Not
# project content and not reproducible from it.
supabase/.temp/
# Operator's notebook — bundle ids, EAS/ASC identifiers, run commands. Kept
# out of git on purpose: it lives on each machine that operates the app.
NOTES.local.md
# Store screenshots — 45 MB of simulator captures for App Store Connect, not
# reproducible *from* the repo but re-shootable *by* it: `docs/store/listing.md`
# records the device and the keystroke. Nothing here reads them, git stores
# PNGs whole, and .git is 55 MB — they would nearly double every clone to
# version files whose only home that matters is App Store Connect.
store-screenshots/
# Local hand-off and Maestro results — bundles, PR drafts, and each smoke
# run's report, logs and screenshots (see app/.maestro/smoke.sh). Machine-
# local by nature, and a failure screenshot can show a signed-in account.
.smoke-local/
